@@s047 At the exam
@@s048 At the exam
@@s049 When the question asks for the <b>minimum number of steps</b> (or of moves, or of arcs) on a graph without weights, the answer is BFS. Write: <i>"Run BFS from s. The first time a node is discovered it is reached by a shortest path, because the queue processes nodes in non-decreasing distance. Time O(n + m)."</i>
@@s050 Typical mistake: writing DFS. The DFS finds <i>a</i> path, not the shortest one.
